#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261" :question/math-academy-id "e-4790" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/0e6491c477a442fc9dae1462413d593815a6761393ad3a0d2f8d72de665a7c93.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "13ebde04-8518-5837-9420-c9487debc562" :question/math-academy-id "e-4791" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/e9e0ea8fb6e9ba5f4595f15efe4f04e93db373dbc020f5672db34d5a3c12024b.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" :question/worked-solution "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "d9beff9d-db58-540f-811e-a07fb77d3d92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6191" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/4749f1e50cf7768f39d26737bfce4d9e8e85d5b350f4bc9844a358cd4c3c5cc0.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/a4e5c5eba6d2d8b30955668d47bb2a131c702cc7ec62ef7dada9ed9ad60d8182.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "896ea9d6-d71a-55be-b137-a5e8ac75f68b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321255} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} {:answer/id #uuid "1176f2ad-3206-5c46-9a89-46355b922602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321257} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4f0f10-e223-5ad9-92de-237ec6ada06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321258} {:answer/id #uuid "0ccb8b67-8dc0-5b12-86be-ddd6cb929af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a6f583-b3f7-5ed3-b22e-5a4039b73977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a8f533b-003a-5522-aad6-99090100d40d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105152" :question/problem "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} {:answer/id #uuid "7a5fc2fa-5f72-5ad0-8fd1-69aef1192d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321298} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5d0608-98d6-5575-8b82-82ab03f3b03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321299} {:answer/id #uuid "f20cb265-08c1-578b-9e9d-7fea1f9cb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321300} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c0a5e-f0ac-5af4-9e4c-4aca14345995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} :answer-field/id #uuid "e62db11a-3245-5286-acf2-e78cc28d847e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49d86e24-f480-5ade-b4df-5af4f350fca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34242" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a729f364-6e1f-5f3c-8aac-bad6ac301733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118174} {:answer/id #uuid "d4202c24-f6d4-545b-8aba-4b4b3d5ccbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118175} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0821b9-32ad-5173-99fe-5be909f0e46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118176} {:answer/id #uuid "52425281-c631-56c6-9881-021bd2376c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118177} {:answer/id #uuid "6a747503-e283-5be3-a6e7-56347bfe62d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4202c24-f6d4-545b-8aba-4b4b3d5ccbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118175} :answer-field/id #uuid "02e1fd9c-0606-50c7-aadd-cc07a38a34d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118173}] :question/id #uuid "14248ec5-b54c-565b-8b43-275a9e097f62" :question/math-academy-id "q-34568" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$c_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}, c_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, d = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf $x_{1}c_{1} + x_{2}c_{2} = d$, then what is $x_{1} + x_{2}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec209f6-9f67-5be4-a1e5-a058b0c97e42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321311} {:answer/id #uuid "4cae1f17-e703-5cbd-b52f-ebdb2959db84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321312} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2abbb8-30d6-5419-81df-961c80bd67f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321313} {:answer/id #uuid "515df100-2311-55f6-84d3-5b2b3c2cddd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321314} {:answer/id #uuid "01273b43-df1c-5f5b-a6c8-eec678b2dff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cae1f17-e703-5cbd-b52f-ebdb2959db84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321312} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f49771-acfd-5c3a-aeaf-c2fd40d7b5b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aada095f-b604-55ca-adb1-bafdd7c5b85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34602" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-2k=24\\,⟹\\,k=-12.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that \n $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240d5547-f75a-5217-a337-31ed278a378b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321318} {:answer/id #uuid "8334a2a9-9569-515a-8062-f982ee8c163c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321319} {:answer/id #uuid "31d57cf9-5e7a-5f99-8bef-908e67dea7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321320} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4282fc-1a7a-5917-896a-a286112f6957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321321} {:answer/id #uuid "d30c39d8-471d-5cb9-9a9a-5833d6fddc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d57cf9-5e7a-5f99-8bef-908e67dea7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321320} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3022814-08a0-5872-9a60-95a62167c0ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8eb567c3-b45a-5792-98ad-b502b4836a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-73931" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29475f1b-ddc2-5713-a560-ff80acf114a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321332} {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} {:answer/id #uuid "279fa3c9-cd8e-53ce-bcf5-08f02de7d37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321334} {:answer/id #uuid "82e88e8d-cabf-599f-abaa-d031639540b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321335} {:answer/id #uuid "125e02f4-7360-5425-9504-fbee83158e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c395a36-ec62-59c1-ab1e-9dee4bd9949b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4aa4d92-2f8e-50b3-bd53-f6e46489ca0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73951" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e1e9a2-153d-517b-ab67-7837c2168555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321339} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1b1e93-7840-5a85-a773-ae87f2b5dd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321340} {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} {:answer/id #uuid "c9dc09a7-17e3-52a0-b09e-3b562d4778e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321342} {:answer/id #uuid "e027474a-a491-5523-a95b-98e263653e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} :answer-field/id #uuid "b90369b5-0596-5750-b1d1-222b297e0373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49280f22-8d86-589c-8580-452aa67d8a42" :question/math-academy-id "q-73952" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbc964ce-7179-5d39-90b8-63ab4b6a71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321360} {:answer/id #uuid "b95f7d8c-a8d1-5fdc-8f38-7bb4d379a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321361} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2fd9b2-0430-5909-bccb-e8612211f708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321362} {:answer/id #uuid "467e0bdc-9778-54b0-9938-f8de39e30cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321363} {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4413af7-ca5e-52fa-8023-3a23c164b23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54baa5a4-47af-54e2-a17a-a1381c32da92" :question/math-academy-id "q-74032" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$"}]}
